{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game game","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game.md","fileName":"Game.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Game Mechanics and Rules]] · [[Game Definition and Forms]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Mechanics and Rules","Game Definition and Forms","Game-Player System","Game Model","Feedback","Player Mental Model","Play","Pretending","Game Goal","Game Rule","advancedgamedesign.pdf","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game game","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game.md","fileName":"Game.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game","heading":"Game","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A game is a voluntary activity organized within a distinct rule-bound context, with goals, meaningful choices or conflict, and a recognizable outcome. Individual examples may not exhibit every trait equally, so games are better treated as a family of related forms than as a rigid checklist.\n\nA functioning game is not only rules or content. It is a [[Game-Player System]] in which a player acts on a dynamic [[Game Model]], receives [[Feedback]], and builds a [[Player Mental Model]] through play.\n\nThe source identifies four essential elements: [[Play]], [[Pretending]], at least one arbitrary and nontrivial [[Game Goal]], and [[Game Rule|rules]]. These elements distinguish a game from an unstructured toy, a purely practical task, or a passive presentation.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Mechanics and Rules","Game Definition and Forms","Game-Player System","Game Model","Fee